# The `tabular-center::dead-column` fixture: an action no state responds to.
#
# `Refund` is IGNORE in every row, which is the lint. Everything else is shaped
# to stay quiet so this fixture says one thing:
#
#   - every row has a HANDLE or a GO, so no `dead-row` and no `no-static-exit`
#   - a HANDLE is present, so the matrix is not fully static and
#     `no-static-entry` does not apply
#   - 6 of 9 cells IGNORE is 66%, under `ignoreHeavyPercent` (70) -- close on
#     purpose, because a fixture that sits at 20% would not notice a
#     threshold moved to 50
#   - no UNREACHABLE cells, so `unreachable-heavy` stays silent
#
# A vending machine that was built with a refund button and never wired it up,
# which is what this lint is for: the matrix makes the omission visible where a
# hand-written dispatcher would just never mention it.

machine Vend
initial Idle
states  Idle Charged Dispensing
actions Insert Select Refund

Idle       | HANDLE   | IGNORE | IGNORE
Charged    | IGNORE   | HANDLE | IGNORE
Dispensing | GO(Idle) | IGNORE | IGNORE
